    "Description": "In this course, IoT technology will be applied to the implementation of a real project by using the relevant knowledge. The application of IoT technology in the course through information technology research and application issues includes the steps of collection user requirements, data, analysis and implementation of an IoT project in real life. related to the agricultural sector. The implementation steps will include design, implementation, testing and demonstration related to the field of IoT for agriculture.",
    "StudentTasks": "- Register the IoT project related to agriculture, - Build the team & select/define the project topic with arrangement/guide from the teacher - Select the team leader and using the FPT account (@fpt.edu.vn account) to setup/configure the project managemernt environment (sources, tasks, issues, milestones) on the GitLab & project documents management on the OneDrive. - Get the detailed assignment from the teacher, plan the project tasks, and execute the project accordingly - Students must attend at least 80% of contact slots in order to be accepted to the final examination. - Student is responsible to do all exercises, assignments and labs given by instructor in class or at home and submit on time - Use laptop in class only for learning purpose Student is responsible to do all exercises given by the teacher in class or at home and submit on time - Using the GitLab to collaborate in every phase of the project by all the team members - Promptly access to the FU LMS at https://flm.fpt.edu.vn/ for up-to-date course information",
    "Tools": "",
    "Scoring Scale": "10",
    "DecisionNo MM/dd/yyyy": "358/QĐ-ĐHFPT dated 04/03/2024",
    "IsApproved": "True",
    "Note": "1) On-going Assessment: 60% - Report 1: Project Introduction: 5% - Report 2: Project Management Plan: 5% - Report 3: Review Related Works and Bibliography: 10% - Report 4: System modeling and operation : 30% - Report 5: Results and Discussion: 10% 2) Final Project Presentation: 40% - Documentation: 10% - Analysis and evaluation results of the project: 20% - Soft Skills: 10% 3) Final Result: 100% Final Project Presentation Criteria: * On-going Assessment Grade >=5/10 * All detailed assessment item's grades > 0/10 Completion Criteria: 1. Project Presentation >=4/10 * Grade >=4/10 * Students can prove that they create the product themselves * No fatal defect in software product (the students can't demonstrate) 2. Final Result >=50",
    "Is Scored": "True",
